L0514: Imported Rust feature is not usable yet

The native item exists and is retained for inspection, but Locus cannot currently use its type or operation. The diagnostic identifies the missing capability. Initial calls support safe non-generic free functions over bool, supported machine integers and tuples. Native types, references, traits, constants, async, unsafe, generics and macros need further checking rules.

Importing a module with such members is permitted; only their use is rejected. Inspect the complete interface with `locus import dependency --json`. A small physical Rust wrapper can expose a supported signature, but it does not establish any proof or effect promise.

```text prose cargo-fixture-diagnostic
import dependency::future;
fn call() -> u8 { future() } // async execution is unavailable.
```

Language, as built: [1.30:5](../spec/19-native-imports.md).
